RELEASE NOTES, c3p0-0.11.0
==========================

The main new feature of c3p0-0.11.0 is fuller support of Java 21+ "loom" virtual
threads. While as of c3p0-0.10.x, c3p0 itself supported relying on virtual threads
for its internals, c3p0 continued to manage client threads with Java's native
wait()/notify() mechanism, which "pins" virtual threads.

Elements relying on wait()/notify() have been rewritten in terms of
java.util.concurrent.locks.ReentrantLock and its Condition mechanism.

Many thanks to Alex Kormukhin for pointing this out and suggesting the fix.

Other improvements include

  * a long-requested ability to have cancel() called on statements
    automatically closed;
    
  * a double-check to prevent rare occurrences of NullPointerException on Connection checkout.

  * use jdbc-version sensitive proxies to prevent NoClassDefFoundErrors when proxies compiled
    against newer JDBC versions try to reference e.g. java.sql.ShardingKey


Config parameters added:
------------------------
    cancelAutomaticallyClosedStatements


Deprecated config parameter removed:
------------------------------------
    [none]


